# Dagric OS — Installer
# Calamares: the same friendly graphical installer Debian Live itself ships.
calamares
calamares-settings-debian
# Password-quality dictionary — without it Calamares' password check errors
# out with "error loading dictionary" and blocks EVERY password.
# (Found by the QEMU install run-through test.)
cracklib-runtime
# unsquashfs — Calamares' unpackfs module needs it to copy the live
# filesystem onto the target disk. (Found by the install run-through:
# "Failed to find unsquashfs".)
squashfs-tools
# The installed system's bootloader — BIOS *and* EFI.
# The -bin packages coexist (the grub-pc/grub-efi-amd64 metapackages
# conflict, so we use the underlying pieces): grub2-common provides
# grub-install, the -bin packages provide the i386-pc and x86_64-efi
# targets, and shim-signed + grub-efi-amd64-signed give Secure Boot.
grub2-common
grub-pc-bin
grub-efi-amd64-bin
grub-efi-amd64-signed
shim-signed
# THE NVIDIA DRIVER HELPER IS DEAD CODE UNDER SECURE BOOT WITHOUT THIS.
#
# dagric-drivers detects Secure Boot with `mokutil --sb-state` and, when it is
# on, enrolls the DKMS module's signing key via `update-secureboot-policy
# --enroll-key` (which itself calls mokutil to do the import). mokutil is only a
# RECOMMENDS of shim-signed, and auto/config passes --apt-recommends false, so
# it was dropped from every image. The whole Secure Boot path was unreachable:
# `command -v mokutil` failed, SB read "disabled" on a machine where it is
# enabled, the enrollment walkthrough never fired, and the owner was told "Done,
# reboot" — after which the unsigned nvidia module refuses to load and the screen
# is black. That is the DEFAULT state on the retail Windows laptops this distro
# is sold to migrate. The sibling dagric-hardware-check already reads the
# SecureBoot efivar directly BECAUSE mokutil was missing and its comment says so;
# dagric-drivers needs the tool itself for the enrollment step, so the fix is to
# ship it rather than only work around the detection.
mokutil
efibootmgr
os-prober
# THE EFI install fix: the EFI System Partition is FAT32, so Calamares
# needs mkfs.vfat (dosfstools) to format it. Without this the install
# dies the instant it hits "Create file system 'fat32' on /dev/vda1".
# BIOS installs used btrfs+MBR and never touched FAT, which is why they
# passed. (Root-caused from Calamares' session.log during the UEFI test.)
dosfstools
# GPT partitioning tools for the EFI/GPT layout (gdisk backend + parted).
gdisk
parted
# btrfs is the default install filesystem (instant Timeshift/rollback
# snapshots); the installed system needs the tools
btrfs-progs
# Full-disk encryption: cryptsetup (userspace) is already pulled in, but the
# initramfs integration is what actually UNLOCKS an encrypted root at boot.
# Without it a LUKS install boots to a dead prompt. Required for the Calamares
# "Encrypt system" option to produce a bootable machine.
cryptsetup-initramfs
